WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.120
Today, many Americans don't like capitalism.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.780
Socialism would be better, they say.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:09.040
Not repressive Russian or Venezuelan socialism,

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.300
but democratic socialism

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.880
like what's practiced in Scandinavia.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.720
I think we should look to countries

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.540
like Denmark,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.320
like Sweden.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.940
Say why, do you want to be like Sweden?

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:20.840
Kinda.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:21.960
Sounds pretty good.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.200
People interviewed in this

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.780
just released PBS documentary say

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.400
America should be more like Sweden.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.580
It seems like it's like a place that

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.180
like no problems or something.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.620
It is a socialist economy.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.220
Volvos and uh,

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.600
socialized medicine.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.620
Volvo

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.240
is now a Chinese company.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.680
Welcome to Stockholm, Sweden.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.300
My name is Johan Norberg

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.280
and this is where I was born and raised.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.520
Johan Norberg made this documentary

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.940
because he wanted to set the record straight.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:56.980
Sweden is not socialist

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:57.820
because the government

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.320
doesn't own the means of production.

00:00:59.322 --> 00:01:00.410
To see that you have to go to

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.020
Venezuela or to Cuba or North Korea.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.660
But we did have a period in the 1970s and

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.760
1980s when we had something

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.580
that resembled socialism.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:10.520
A big government

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.120
that taxed and spend heavily

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.080
and that's the period in Swedish history

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.500
when our economy was going south.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.100
So much so that even socialists complained about the

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:21.860
high taxes.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:22.500
Astrid Lindgren,

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.100
who wrote the very popular children's books

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.540
Pippi Longstocking for instance,

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.910
she was a social democrat but she had made a lot

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.300
of money from her books.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.420
She found that she paid 102% in taxes.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.340
She wrote this angry essay

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:39.860
about a witch who was quite mean and vicious,

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:42.660
but not at all as vicious as the Swedish tax authorities.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.360
And yet even though taxes were high,

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.400
they did not bring in enough money

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.620
to fund Sweden's welfare state.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.555
There were waiting lines to get health care,

00:01:50.555 --> 00:01:52.160
people couldn't get the pension

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.162
that they thought that they depended on for the future.

00:01:55.162 --> 00:01:56.240
At that point

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.040
the Swedish population just said,

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.920
enough we can't do this.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:01.940
Sweden then reduced

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.166
government's role.

00:02:03.166 --> 00:02:05.400
They cut public spending,

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.560
privatized the national rail network,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.000
abolished certain government monopolies,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.120
eliminated inheritance taxes,

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.920
and sold state-owned businesses

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.520
like the maker of Absolut Vodka.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.780
Lower taxes reformed the pension system

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.680
so that it wasn't unsustainable.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.957
The results from the

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.240
spending cuts and privatization?

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.380
This impoverished peasant nation

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.700
developed into one of the world's richest countries.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:34.340
All I hear is that Sweden is this socialist paradise.

00:02:34.346 --> 00:02:35.620
We do have a bigger

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.120
welfare state than the U.S.,

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.200
higher taxes than the U.S.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.620
But in other areas,

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:41.260
when it comes to free markets,

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:42.324
when it comes to competition,

00:02:42.324 --> 00:02:43.800
when it comes to free trade,

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.060
Sweden is actually more free market.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:46.880
That free market

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.380
pays for Sweden's big welfare programs.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.780
Today our taxes pay for pensions.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.780
You call it Social Security.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:58.140
For 18 month paid parental leave,

00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.940
government paid childcare,

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.300
for working families,

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:01.980
but

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.020
having the government manage all of these things

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.440
didn't work well

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.380
so we had to manage it in another way.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.720
They privatized.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.290
We realized in Sweden that

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.460
with these government monopolies,

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.970
we don't get the innovation that we get

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.170
when we have competition

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.040
and this is particularly true for the school system.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.700
Sweden switched to a school voucher system

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.080
that lets parents pick their kids' school,

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.760
and forces schools to compete.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.300
And one of the results that we've seen is

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.911
not just that the private schools

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.460
are better than the public ones,

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.060
but even the

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.660
public schools in the vicinity of private schools,

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:39.900
they often improve

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.380
because they have to.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:44.170
Sweden's version of Social Security was going broke,

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:46.260
so Sweden privatized that, too.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.320
Privatize the pension system?

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.020
That terrifies people.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.680
And obviously that scares people,

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.319
but when they realize that the alternative

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.840
was that the whole pension system would collapse,

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:56.950
they thought that this is much

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:58.440
better than nothing.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.320
Now the bulk of pensions

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.900
is really

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.600
contribution defined.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.160
So if things are going well for Sweden

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.920
pensions are increasing,

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.820
but if things are going less well,

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:12.260
pensions are automatically lowered,

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:15.240
which basically takes away from politicians

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.800
the ability to buy votes

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.600
by just promising higher pensions

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.900
and letting future generations pay.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.700
And when it comes to taxes,

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.940
what Sweden does may surprise you.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:27.840
The low income earners in Sweden

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.560
pay a lot more than

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:30.740
low income earners

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:31.400
in America.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.660
So despite the fact that Sweden looks

00:04:33.669 --> 00:04:35.420
like sort of a socialist country

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.860
which taxes rich exorbitantly high,

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.260
the truth is the opposite.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:41.740
People who earn below average income

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.540
pay up to 60% in taxes.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.440
This is the dirty little secret

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.060
about the Swedish tax system.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.100
We don't take from the rich

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.540
and give to the poor.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.900
We squeeze the poor

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.900
because they are loyal taxpayers.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.800
Not taking more from the rich,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.117
school choice,

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.700
privatization,

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:02.880
Sweden is anything but socialist.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.260
You can't turn your backs to the well,

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:07.320
to the creation of wealth.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.386
You can watch the full documentary

00:05:09.386 --> 00:05:11.420
Sweden: Lessons for America?

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.460
at free to choose.TV.

